## Interface: 16001
## Title: Mint Community Tools
## Notes: The in-game side of Minty's Community Manager. Exports your gear and talents for the guild website's Roster page, keeps a log of what drops, and can give the game a flat, minimalist UI: action bars, chat, unit frames and a square minimap, each optional.
## Author: Zack
## Version: 0.5.0
## SavedVariables: MintCommunityToolsDB
## IconTexture: Interface\Icons\INV_Misc_Note_01
## X-License: MIT
## X-Website: https://github.com/wongz1/mint-community-tools
## X-Curse-Project-ID: 1724233

# 16001 = WoW Forever beta client 1.60.1 (major * 10000 + minor * 100 + patch). Other addons
# with this number load on the beta client without "out of date" warnings. To read the real
# number in game:  /mint debug   (or /run print((select(4, GetBuildInfo()))) ).
# If the addon ever shows as out of date after a patch, tick "Load out of date AddOns" on the
# AddOns screen at character select.

# Saved.lua works around a WoW Forever beta bug: the client writes addon data to
# WTF/Account/<account>/SavedVariables/MintCommunityTools.lua but never reads it back. When
# Saved.lua is a link to that file (LinkSavedSettings.cmd on Windows, link-saved-settings.sh on
# macOS/Linux), the last save is loaded here as code, so the loot log survives a logout. It is
# fine for the file to be missing: the game skips it. Once Blizzard fixes the loader, the real
# data loads afterwards and takes over.
Saved.lua
Encode.lua
